PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The clinical vignette outlines an elderly patient with mania and epilepsy whose medication adjustments culminate in Stevens-Johnson syndrome/toxic epidermal necrolysis, pointing specifically to the interaction between valproate and lamotrigine or aromatic anticonvulsant bioactivation. The deliberation remains focused on two complementary interpretations of the initiating biochemical reaction: the upstream pharmacokinetic trigger via inhibition of glucuronidation (catalyzed by UDP-glucuronosyltransferase) and the downstream bioactivation reaction involving cytochrome P450-mediated epoxidation to a reactive arene oxide intermediate. Maintaining both glucuronidation (inhibition of glucuronide conjugation) and aromatic epoxidation ensures complete coverage of the pharmacokinetic and immunotoxicological mechanisms.
}

